[{"location":"#IDRBindingDataset","page":"Home","title":"IDRBindingDataset","text":"Documentation for IDRBindingDataset.\n\n","category":"section"},{"location":"#IDRBindingDataset._attempt_download-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString, Function, Function, Bool}","page":"Home","title":"IDRBindingDataset._attempt_download","text":"download_to_file_with_retries(url, destination;\n    delays = ExponentialBackOff(n = 5), downloader = Downloads.download,\n    logger = println, log_success = true)\n\nDownload url into destination using atomic writes and bounded retries. If all attempts fail, the last exception is rethrown.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"#IDRBindingDataset.build_disprot_regions_url-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Home","title":"IDRBindingDataset.build_disprot_regions_url","text":"build_disprot_regions_url(release)\n\nBuild the DisProt API URL for retrieving all entries of a release, including ambiguous regions and excluding obsolete ones.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"#IDRBindingDataset.clean_directory-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Home","title":"IDRBindingDataset.clean_directory","text":"clean_directory(path)\n\nRemove path recursively if it exists, then recreate it as an empty directory.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"#IDRBindingDataset.download_to_gzip_file_with_retries-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString}","page":"Home","title":"IDRBindingDataset.download_to_gzip_file_with_retries","text":"download_to_gzip_file_with_retries(url, destination;\n    delays = ExponentialBackOff(n = 5), downloader = Downloads.download,\n    logger = println)\n\nDownload url, compress it as gzip, and save it to destination.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"#IDRBindingDataset.ensure_files_within_size_limit-Tuple{Any}","page":"Home","title":"IDRBindingDataset.ensure_files_within_size_limit","text":"ensure_files_within_size_limit(paths; max_bytes, limit_name, remediation)\n\nValidate that all files in paths exist and are smaller than or equal to max_bytes.\n\nIf any file is missing or exceeds the configured limit, this function throws an ErrorException with a clear multi-line diagnostic.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"#IDRBindingDataset.remove_files-Tuple{Any}","page":"Home","title":"IDRBindingDataset.remove_files","text":"remove_files(paths)\n\nRemove each file path in paths if it exists. Parent directories are kept.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"#IDRBindingDataset.utc_now_iso8601-Tuple{}","page":"Home","title":"IDRBindingDataset.utc_now_iso8601","text":"utc_now_iso8601(; clock = () -> now(UTC))\n\nReturn the current UTC timestamp as yyyy-mm-ddTHH:MM:SSZ.\n\nThe clock keyword is injectable to make tests deterministic.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"#IDRBindingDataset.write_download_report-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Home","title":"IDRBindingDataset.write_download_report","text":"write_download_report(report_path; status, timestamp_utc, release, idpo_version,\n    sources, error_message = nothing)\n\nWrite a Markdown report describing the last raw-data download run.\n\nsources must be an iterable of (url, filename) pairs where each filename is expected to live in dirname(report_path).\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"}]
